{"id": 20, "ts": 1780587029.4336576, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to shift my recommendation to Candidate\u202fC.\u202fJames just confirmed that C \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d giving us concrete evidence of stress resilience\u2014a key safety criterion that was previously missing for C. Combined with the fact that C is 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, we now have a solid picture of both reliability and crew cooperation for C.\nIn contrast, we still have no direct evidence of Candidate\u202fB\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, and Emily notes only a general concern that B can be pretentious and adopt the wrong tone, suggesting communication issues that could affect teamwork. While B\u2019s conscientiousness and stress handling remain strong, the lack of proven crew\u2011cooperation and the documented communication weaknesses make his overall fit less certain than C\u2019s now\u2011demonstrated strengths.\nTherefore, based on the newly available stress\u2011resilience evidence and the positive crew dynamic, I would vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
