{"id": 25, "ts": 1780587063.1532884, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I concur with James and Emily\u2019s assessment that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s demonstrated calmness in a crisis, 100\u202f% reliability, and ability to create a positive crew atmosphere give him a solid, well\u2011rounded profile for the long\u2011distance pilot role. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while conscientious and technically strong, still has unresolved concerns about crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication that could undermine safety in a multi\u2011crew environment. Candidate\u202fA lacks any evidence on stress resilience, decision quality, or crew interaction, and his noted difficulty taking criticism and occasional disorganization raise reliability questions. Candidate\u202fD, although responsible and good at problem\u2011solving, is described as arrogant with weak leadership, which may impair cockpit teamwork. Given the current evidence, I maintain my vote for Candidate\u202fC, while we should still seek any missing data on A and D before finalizing."}
