{"id": 29, "ts": 1780587100.0858011, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s calmness and crew atmosphere, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit.\u202fB\u2019s record shows very high operational reliability (very conscientious) and proven stress resilience (handles stress very well), plus concrete technical strengths\u2014accurate weather assessment and excellent computer skills\u2014that are critical for long\u2011distance operations. While B\u2019s pretentiousness and occasional tone issues are concerning, they are behavioral traits we can address through targeted crew\u2011resource\u2011training, and they do not undermine his demonstrated competence. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC, although calm, has notable gaps: difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric reputation, and a reluctance to pursue further education, which raise doubts about his adaptability and long\u2011term development in a safety\u2011critical role. Moreover, we still lack evidence of C\u2019s technical competence, whereas B\u2019s technical judgment is well\u2011documented. Given the current evidence and the ability to mitigate B\u2019s communication concerns, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
